I may be ignorant of the good way to do this, so maybe somebody else can chime in if this is already built in.

But one option would be to leverage the session$onSessionEnded feature (a la https://github.com/trestletech/ShinyChat/blob/master/server.R#L30) which defines a function that executes when a *session* ends. Obviously, you would have to define a bit of a wrapper around this to figure out whether or not the *application* should be disconnected.

But perhaps something like this would get the job done in server.R (pardon any syntax errors, I'm just eyeballing this)

## server.R

vals <- reactiveValues(sessions = 0, connection = NULL)

shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {
  observe({
    # This observer will get executed once on session startup, so increment
    isolate({
      vals$sessions <- vals$sessions + 1
    })
  })

session$onSessionEnded(function() {
    isolate({
      # This will get executed when a session exits
      vals$sessions <- vals$sessions - 1
    })
  })
observe({
# This just takes a reactive dependency on vals$session, so when that number
# changes this function will execute. If sessions is now 0, disconnect. If it's
# non-zero, make sure we're connected
if (vals$sessions == 0){
if (!is.null(vals$connection)){
# We have a connection but no sessions, disconnect.
disconnect()
vals$connection <- NULL
}
} else {
if (is.null(vals$connection)){
# We have a session but no connection, open the connection
vals$connection <- openConnection()
}
}
})
})

